WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.120
Is netrin a gradient spreading from the midline, or a path laid down along the way?

2
00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:13.660
Return to the map: the floor plate at the bottom, the progenitors around the canal.

3
00:00:14.733 --> 00:00:19.013
Start in a dish. A growth cone compares the cue on its two sides.

4
00:00:20.017 --> 00:00:24.057
Around a small source, like a bead, concentration falls with distance.

5
00:00:25.117 --> 00:00:29.597
The fractional difference across a growth cone is roughly its width over its

6
00:00:29.597 --> 00:00:30.597
distance from the source.

7
00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:34.940
Close in, a growth cone sees about a ten percent difference.

8
00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:38.000
A millimetre away, about one percent.

9
00:00:38.833 --> 00:00:42.413
But a growth cone measures bound receptors, not netrin itself.

10
00:00:43.483 --> 00:00:46.923
The Kd is the concentration that fills half the receptors.

11
00:00:48.083 --> 00:00:53.103
Give it the same ten percent difference at three backgrounds: far below the Kd, at

12
00:00:53.103 --> 00:00:56.383
it, far above. Where is the bound difference largest?

13
00:01:02.417 --> 00:01:07.537
At the Kd. Far below it, almost no receptors are bound on either side.

14
00:01:08.517 --> 00:01:09.817
Far above it, almost all are.

15
00:01:13.217 --> 00:01:16.957
Binding is noisy, because molecules arrive and leave at random.

16
00:01:17.817 --> 00:01:19.597
A tiny difference is easily lost.

17
00:01:20.617 --> 00:01:23.737
A fixed detector gets the most signal near its Kd.

18
00:01:24.637 --> 00:01:29.257
Adapting, by resetting its baseline, lets the growth cone respond again as the

19
00:01:29.257 --> 00:01:30.257
background changes.

20
00:01:31.077 --> 00:01:32.697
It cannot remove the binding limit.

21
00:01:33.650 --> 00:01:36.950
Now the embryo, where netrin-1 is made in two places.

22
00:01:38.050 --> 00:01:39.950
Floor plate cells make it.

23
00:01:40.270 --> 00:01:44.090
So do progenitors across a broad stretch of the ventricular zone.

24
00:01:45.133 --> 00:01:47.893
The progenitors send netrin out along their fibres.

25
00:01:48.873 --> 00:01:52.473
It builds up at the pial surface, along the commissural axons' path.

26
00:01:53.467 --> 00:01:55.467
So there are two candidate ways to guide.

27
00:01:56.367 --> 00:01:58.867
One is a gradient diffusing from the floor plate.

28
00:01:59.687 --> 00:02:00.887
That is chemotropism.

29
00:02:01.867 --> 00:02:05.487
Guidance by netrin held on a surface is called haptotaxis.

30
00:02:06.567 --> 00:02:12.227
In 2017, two groups deleted the netrin-1 gene from one source at a time, in mice.

31
00:02:13.167 --> 00:02:16.547
A conditional deletion removes a gene only in chosen cells.

32
00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:22.040
If a floor plate gradient did most of the guiding, which deletion should cause more

33
00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:23.040
errors?

34
00:02:28.483 --> 00:02:30.123
The floor plate deletion should.

35
00:02:31.043 --> 00:02:35.963
It did not. Without floor plate netrin, most commissural axons stayed on course.

36
00:02:37.017 --> 00:02:40.877
Without progenitor netrin, many commissural axons went off course.

37
00:02:41.817 --> 00:02:44.437
A third study found the same pattern in the hindbrain.

38
00:02:47.950 --> 00:02:51.950
A deletion shows which source the axons need, not how they read it.

39
00:02:52.570 --> 00:02:54.730
A path and a short-range gradient both fit.

40
00:02:55.700 --> 00:02:57.320
Nor is the floor plate idle.

41
00:02:58.180 --> 00:03:01.960
In the spinal cord, later studies found that its netrin still contributes.

42
00:03:03.050 --> 00:03:08.070
So, much of the netrin that matters seems to act near where progenitors lay it down.

43
00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:11.370
That holds in the mouse spinal cord and hindbrain.

44
00:03:12.290 --> 00:03:14.670
In the spinal cord, the floor plate keeps a part.

45
00:03:15.633 --> 00:03:18.413
After crossing, the axons do not turn back.

46
00:03:19.273 --> 00:03:21.473
What changes in the reader is the next lesson.

47
00:03:22.467 --> 00:03:27.267
The takeaway: netrin marks a place, and the growth cone decides what to do there.
